From: NGM <ngm@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ngm-fix: GH-25089 heap over-read via crafted alias size in zip-based phar

What: phar_parse_zipfile() set the phar's alias length from the size the ZIP
headers CLAIM for .phar/alias.txt, before reading it. The alias buffer only
holds what was actually read (decompressed), so a crafted archive claiming a
larger size made phar_validate_alias() and Phar::getAlias() read past the
heap buffer. Set the length after the read, from the bytes actually read.

Why ours: upstream fixed it on 2026-11-01 (php-src 61edcf9b, PHP-8.4 and up,
not yet released, no CVE). Every legacy minor has the same code, and it is
reachable from outside: opening an uploaded file as phar:// / PharData is
enough. A one-line move, same as upstream; test is upstream's gh25089.phpt
with --EXTENSIONS-- turned into --SKIPIF-- for the old run-tests.

Behaviour change: none for valid archives; a crafted one now gets its real
alias instead of reading past the buffer.

Delete when: the CloudLinux series for this minor carries the fix (an
apply-time reject on this hunk says so).
---
--- a/ext/phar/zip.c
+++ b/ext/phar/zip.c
@@ -575,7 +575,6 @@
 			fp->readpos = 0;
 			/* the above lines should be for php < 5.2.6 after 5.3 filters are fixed */
 
-			mydata->alias_len = entry.uncompressed_filesize;
 			if (entry.flags & PHAR_ENT_COMPRESSED_GZ) {
 				filter = php_stream_filter_create("zlib.inflate", NULL, php_stream_is_persistent(fp));
 
@@ -660,6 +659,9 @@
 				}
 			}
 
+			/* Only now: the size the headers claim may exceed what was read. */
+			mydata->alias_len = entry.uncompressed_filesize;
+
 			/* return to central directory parsing */
 			php_stream_seek(fp, saveloc, SEEK_SET);
 		}
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ext/phar/tests/zip/gh25089.phpt
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+--TEST--
+GH-25089 (Heap buffer over-read via crafted alias size in zip-based phar)
+--SKIPIF--
+<?php
+if (!extension_loaded("phar")) die("skip phar extension not loaded");
+if (!extension_loaded("zlib")) die("skip zlib extension not loaded");
+?>
+--FILE--
+<?php
+$name = '.phar/alias.txt';
+$alias = 'ABCD';
+$data = gzdeflate($alias);
+$crc = crc32($alias);
+$claimed = 0x1000;
+
+$local = "PK\x03\x04"
+    . pack('vvvvvVVVvv', 20, 0, 8, 0, 0,
+        $crc, strlen($data), $claimed, strlen($name), 0)
+    . $name . $data;
+$central = "PK\x01\x02"
+    . pack('vvvvvvVVVvvvvvVV', 20, 20, 0, 8, 0, 0,
+        $crc, strlen($data), $claimed, strlen($name), 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
+    . $name;
+$end = "PK\x05\x06"
+    . pack('vvvvVVv', 0, 0, 1, 1, strlen($central), strlen($local), 0);
+
+file_put_contents(dirname(__FILE__) . '/gh25089.zip', $local . $central . $end);
+
+$phar = new PharData(dirname(__FILE__) . '/gh25089.zip');
+var_dump($phar->getAlias());
+?>
+--CLEAN--
+<?php
+@unlink(dirname(__FILE__) . '/gh25089.zip');
+?>
+--EXPECT--
+string(4) "ABCD"
